15 0 obj
<< /A 39 0 R /Alt (Flowchart of a neural network model with three main sections: the Dual Branch Representation Block, Cross Attention Block, and Classifier. EEG and peripheral signals undergo preprocessing and proceed through convolutional and max-pooling layers. The Cross Attention Block includes connections labeled Q, K, and V. The Classifier outputs a graph and categorized images for emotions: Happy, Sad, Neutral, and Fear.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 30 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 40 0 R /Alt (Flowchart depicting a study design consisting of three sessions. Each session includes multiple trials, numbered from one to fifteen. In each trial, a sequence occurs: a start hint, watching a film clip classified as happy, sad, neutral, or fear, a self-assessment, and a rest period. Sessions proceed sequentially from one to three.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 31 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 41 0 R /Alt (Diagram showing electrode placements for EEG studies. The left diagram, labeled SEED-IV, features numerous electrode positions arranged in a dense grid. The right diagram, labeled DEAP, displays a more sparse arrangement with fewer electrodes. Both layouts depict a top-down view of a head with markings like FP1, AF3, F3, FZ, and more, indicating specific electrode sites.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 32 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 42 0 R /Alt (Line graph showing accuracy and loss for emotion recognition over 120 epochs. The blue line represents accuracy, increasing steadily to about 0.95. The red line represents loss, which decreases consistently to about 0.1. Accuracy and loss converge around epoch 20 before diverging.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 34 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 43 0 R /Alt (Bar chart comparing accuracy percentages of Valence and Arousal across 32 subjects. Valence, shown in blue, and Arousal, in orange, exhibit similar high accuracy around 80% to 100% for most subjects.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 35 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 44 0 R /Alt (Scatter plot showing two panels. The left panel, titled \215The original feature,\216 displays a random, dense cluster of multicolored points. The right panel, titled \215The learned representation,\216 shows distinct, color-coded clusters. The points are separated into yellow, green, blue, and purple clusters, indicating clearer categorization.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 36 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
21 0 obj
<< /A 45 0 R /Alt (Two confusion matrices compare valence and arousal predictions. The valence matrix shows true negative at 98.08 percent and positive at 90.91 percent. The arousal matrix shows true negative at 96.02 percent and positive at 94.21 percent.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 36 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
